Given, \[V_{\text{bus}}=100\,\text{kV rms},\qquad C_1=1\,\mu\text{F}\pm10\%,\qquad C_2=9\,\mu\text{F}\pm10\%\] The output is taken across \(C_2\). <span class="missing-fig">[figure unavailable]</span> For series capacitors, \[V_{\text{out}}=V_{\text{bus}}\frac{X_{C2}}{X_{C1}+X_{C2}}\] Since \(X_C=\frac{1}{\omega C}\), \[V_{\text{out}}=V_{\text{bus}}\frac{\frac{1}{C_2}}{\frac{1}{C_1}+\frac{1}{C_2}}
=V_{\text{bus}}\frac{C_1}{C_1+C_2}\] To maximize \(V_{\text{out}}\), take \(C_1\) maximum and \(C_2\) minimum: \[C_{1,\max}=1.1\,\mu\text{F},\qquad C_{2,\min}=8.1\,\mu\text{F}\] Thus, \[V_{\text{out,max}}=100\frac{1.1}{1.1+8.1}
=100\frac{1.1}{9.2}
=11.9565\,\text{kV}\] \[\boxed{11.96}\]

